# SRG-APP-000760-AU-000150  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement an audit reduction capability that
# supports after-the-fact investigations of incidents.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000760-AU-000150
group:           V-263561
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-003824
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Reduction for an after-the-fact investigation has to reach records still
                 held in the index, so the application's share is both the search-time
                 knowledge layer bound to the audit source types and the retention and
                 archive settings that keep those records reachable.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.
governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.

check:           props.conf [<source type>] present
check:           indexes.conf [_audit] coldToFrozenDir non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          indexes.conf [<index>] coldToFrozenDir https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/indexes.conf
vendor:          indexes.conf [<index>] frozenTimePeriodInSecs https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-indexers-and-indexer-clusters/10.4/back-up-and-archive-your-indexes/set-a-retirement-and-archiving-policy
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The retention period that bounds how far back an investigation can reach
                 is organization-defined and recorded in the site documentation, as product
                 STIG SPLK-CL-000120 check text states.
external:        Capacity and integrity of the frozen archive destination rest on the
                 storage platform and the operating system.
external:        Restoring archived buckets for an investigation is an operator procedure
                 performed outside the running application.
external:        The retention period itself, which is organization-defined: every index
                 declares frozenTimePeriodInSecs, so a test for the key cannot fail, and a
                 test on the value would report a finding against any site that chooses the
                 shipped six years deliberately.
external:        Preservation of frozen audit buckets by a script rather than a directory:
                 indexes.conf coldToFrozenScript is the documented equivalent of
                 coldToFrozenDir, and the two are alternatives, so an instance that uses
                 the script satisfies the objective by other means and the assessor reads
                 which of the two is set.

citation:        props.conf.spec:80 [<spec>], :1085 REPORT-<class>, :1102 EXTRACT-<class>,
                 :1329 LOOKUP-<class>; indexes.conf.spec:684 frozenTimePeriodInSecs, :713
                 coldToFrozenScript, :792 coldToFrozenDir. Product STIG SPLK-CL-000120 fix
                 text, "Set frozenTimePeriodInSecs to the defined retention period for each
                 index location."
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: no knowledge layer is bound to
                 the audit source types in scope, or those indexes state no retention
                 period and no frozen archive destination, so records age out by deletion
                 and the application's audit reduction cannot reach them for an
                 after-the-fact investigation.
